  "inbound_message": "From: Greg Whitmore <greg.whitmore@mailbox.example>\nTo: Aerlink Customer Care <care@aerlink.example>\nDate: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 07:20:33 +0100\nSubject: FW: our correspondence - please action the latest\n\nI am forwarding this entire thread because I have now dealt with four different\npeople and each one has asked me to explain it again from the beginning.\n\nEverything is below, oldest first. Please read to the end and action the latest\none.\n\nGreg Whitmore\n\n========================= FORWARDED CONVERSATION =========================\n(oldest first)\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Greg Whitmore\n    To: Aerlink Bookings\n    Date: Mon, 1 Jun 2026 09:12\n\n    Booking confirmation received for AER-5C9X3T, LHR-GVA on 5 August. Thanks.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Aerlink Bookings\n    To: Greg Whitmore\n    Date: Mon, 1 Jun 2026 09:15\n\n    Thank you for booking with Aerlink. Your confirmation is attached.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Greg Whitmore\n    To: Aerlink Customer Care\n    Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 14:40\n\n    Can I add a checked bag to this booking please?\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Aerlink Customer Care\n    To: Greg Whitmore\n    Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 16:02\n\n    Yes, a 23kg bag has been added. You'll see the charge on your card.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Greg Whitmore\n    To: Aerlink Customer Care\n    Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 08:31\n\n    The charge has gone through twice. Can you look at that.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Aerlink Customer Care\n    To: Greg Whitmore\n    Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 11:55\n\n    Apologies, one of those was an authorisation hold and will drop off in 3-5 days.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Greg Whitmore\n    To: Aerlink Customer Care\n    Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 19:20\n\n    It has dropped off, thanks.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Aerlink Marketing\n    To: Greg Whitmore\n    Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 10:05\n\n    Summer fares to the Alps - book by 31 July. [newsletter]\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Greg Whitmore\n    To: Aerlink Marketing\n    Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 10:07\n\n    Please stop sending me these.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Greg Whitmore\n    To: Aerlink Customer Care\n    Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 13:44\n\n    Can I choose my seat in advance? I'd like an aisle.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Aerlink Customer Care\n    To: Greg Whitmore\n    Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 15:10\n\n    Seat 14C has been allocated to you.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Greg Whitmore\n    To: Aerlink Customer Care\n    Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 07:55\n\n    14C is fine. Thank you.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Aerlink Operations\n    To: Greg Whitmore\n    Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 17:30\n\n    Advance notice: some services on 5 August may be affected by crew availability at LHR.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Greg Whitmore\n    To: Aerlink Customer Care\n    Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 08:00\n\n    What does that notice mean for AK229 on Wednesday? Is it going or not?\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Aerlink Customer Care\n    To: Greg Whitmore\n    Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 12:22\n\n    AK229 is currently scheduled to operate. We will contact you if that changes.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Aerlink Operations\n    To: Greg Whitmore\n    Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 07:34\n\n    AK229 LHR-GVA on 5 August has been cancelled. We are sorry for the disruption.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Greg Whitmore\n    To: Aerlink Customer Care\n    Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 07:51\n\n    You have got to be joking. You told me yesterday it was operating.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Greg Whitmore\n    To: Aerlink Customer Care\n    Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 08:14\n\n    Right. I have had enough of this. CANCEL THE WHOLE BOOKING AND REFUND ME IN FULL.\n    I do not want to be rebooked, I do not want a voucher, I want my money back and I will\n    make my own arrangements. Please confirm the refund has been processed.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Aerlink Customer Care\n    To: Greg Whitmore\n    Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 09:40\n\n    We have received your request. A refund request has been queued for review.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Greg Whitmore\n    To: Aerlink Customer Care\n    Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 14:05\n\n    Further to my phone call just now - please DISREGARD the refund request below.\n    I spoke to one of your colleagues and confirmed it verbally. My sister has offered to\n    drive me to the meeting on Thursday instead, so the Wednesday flight is no longer the\n    issue, but I still need to GET BACK, and I still need to get out there later in the\n    month. Do not refund. I repeat, do NOT refund the booking.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Aerlink Customer Care\n    To: Greg Whitmore\n    Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 14:31\n\n    Understood. The refund request has been withdrawn and no refund will be issued.\n    Your booking remains live.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    From: Greg Whitmore\n    To: Aerlink Customer Care\n    Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:47\n\n    Following up. Nothing has happened since Wednesday and nobody has come back to me.\n\n    What I actually need now, and this is the only thing I need:\n\n    Put me on the earliest Geneva flight you have on MONDAY 10 AUGUST. Same booking,\n    same seat preference if possible. That is all. Please just do that and confirm it.\n\n    I am aware I have sent you a lot of messages. Please action the most recent one.\n\n========================= END OF FORWARDED CONVERSATION =========================\n",
  "decision": {
    "summary": "Greg Whitmore's flight AK229 from LHR to GVA on 5 August 2026 was cancelled due to crew availability issues. Consequently, I have rebooked him on the earliest available flight from London Heathrow (LHR) to Geneva (GVA) on 10 August 2026, which is operated by Air France flight AF557. The booking remains confirmed, and the total fare for this rebooking is \u00a3286.42.\n\nAs for passenger entitlements, upon reviewing the situation, it appears that no statutory compensation is owed, as the cancellation was due to crew issues but does not warrant compensation at this moment according to our records. Additionally, I attempted to issue a hotel voucher for accommodation; however, there was no allocation available for the requested night.\n\nIn summary:\n- **What Greg receives:** A new rebooking on flight AF557 to GVA on 10 August 2026.\n- **Statutory compensation:** \u00a30.00, as no compensation is due.\n- **Hotel voucher:** Not issued due to lack of availability.\n\nThank you, and I hope this resolves Greg\u2019s case satisfactorily.",
